<title>BELGIUM: BELGIUM BANS GERMAN PIG IMPORTS OVER SWINE FEVER.</title>
<headline>BELGIUM BANS GERMAN PIG IMPORTS OVER SWINE FEVER.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium banned all imports of live pigs from Germany on Friday because of fears the animals could be carrying swine fever.</p>
<p>&quot;Each transport of pigs from whatever region of Germany at the moment represents an unacceptably high risk for the Belgian pig sector,&quot; the Agriculture Ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>German authorities have ordered 10,000 pigs to be killed to prevent the spreading of swine fever after the recent discovery of cases in several states.</p>
<p>Hundreds of thousands of pigs were slaughtered in Belgium after an outbreak of swine fever in the early 1990s.</p>
<p>Belgium imports around 50,000 piglets each month from Germany, mainly from southern German states.</p>
